# Inventory of MariaDB/MySQL servers for NOLA to monitor. One line per server.
# generate.sh turns each line into a mysqld_exporter service + a Prometheus target.
#
# Format:   Friendly Name | mysql_address:port | exporter_port
#
#   Friendly Name  shown in the app (becomes the Prometheus `server` label)
#   mysql_address  reachable FROM the exporter container:
#                    - DB published on the holodeck host -> host.docker.internal:<port>
#                    - DB container on a shared docker network -> its container name
#                    - or a LAN IP
#   exporter_port  a unique host port for this exporter (9104, 9105, 9106, ...)
#
# If all your databases live inside ONE MariaDB server, use a SINGLE line — one
# exporter reports every schema on that server.
#
# Edit / delete the examples below:

Minecraft DB | host.docker.internal:3306 | 9104
Rust DB      | host.docker.internal:3307 | 9105
